Settle_Concrete_Test
├── when the caller is not a settler
│   └── it should revert
└── when the caller is a settler
    ├── given the contract is halted
    │   └── it should revert
    └── given the contract is not halted
        ├── when the batch is empty or holds more than 100 ids
        │   └── it should revert
        └── when the batch holds 1 to 100 ids
            ├── when the market does not exist
            │   └── it should revert
            └── when the market exists
                ├── when the price is not positive
                │   └── it should revert
                └── when the price is positive
                    ├── when the tick is more than the clock skew ahead
                    │   └── it should revert
                    └── when the tick is at most the clock skew ahead
                        ├── when an id was never opened
                        │   └── it should revert
                        └── when every id was opened
                            ├── when a position belongs to another market
                            │   └── it should revert
                            └── when every position belongs to the market
                                ├── given a position has already ended
                                │   ├── it should skip it
                                │   └── it should settle the others
                                └── given every position is open
                                    ├── when the tick is not a position's expiry second
                                    │   └── it should revert
                                    └── when the tick is every position's expiry second
                                        ├── when the price touches a position's line
                                        │   └── it should revert
                                        └── when the price touches no line
                                            ├── when a payout has too little gas
                                            │   └── it should revert
                                            └── when every payout has the gas it needs
                                                ├── given the token refuses a payout
                                                │   ├── it should keep the payout for the user to claim
                                                │   └── it should settle the rest of the batch
                                                ├── given the pool cannot pay a profit in full
                                                │   ├── it should pay the profit free money allows
                                                │   ├── it should queue the rest as an IOU
                                                │   └── it should keep the position as owed
                                                └── given the pool can pay every profit
                                                    ├── it should close each position
                                                    ├── it should pay each user the payout, less the fees
                                                    ├── it should accrue the fees once
                                                    ├── it should emit {PositionSettled} for each
                                                    └── it should return the number settled
